{
  "index": 75,
  "text": "It is also important to note that undernutrition is often associated with micronutrient deficiencies [13], as most participants in this study had microcytic anemia (Table 3), whose main etiology is iron deficiency. Low socioeconomic status was also reflected in education level, where over 70% of caretakers had no formal education or only primary education (Table 1); this affects financial status and understanding of child care and nutrition. Poor socioeconomic status can also lead to comorbidities such as intestinal worms, causing recurrent blood loss and anemia, as reported by [14] in Ethiopia.",
